  <content>
  <section><div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="8d3b45f1-7144-47ef-87e0-58326dd9d1e2" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
  <!--1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="91b86a46-3b99-4625-ad43-24e8495050c2" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(a(x)=3x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(d(x)=9+3x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(x)=9 \\cdot 3x\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(a(x)=3x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(b(x)=3^x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c(x)=x^3\\) &quot;, &quot;\\(d(x)=9+3x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(e(x)=9 \\cdot 3^x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(x)=9 \\cdot 3x\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Functions \(a, b, c, d, e\), and \(f\) are given below. Which functions are linear? <emphasis>Select the three</emphasis> answers
          that apply.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.14.1. 
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="7e5c2385-363a-4bc2-b500-8771bcfa0add" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(b(x)=3^x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(e(x)=9\\cdot 3^x\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(a(x)=3x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(b(x)=3^x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c(x)=x^3\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(d(x)=9+3x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(e(x)=9\\cdot 3^x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(x)=9\\cdot 3x\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Functions \(a, b, c, d, e\), and \(f\) are given below. Which functions are exponential? <emphasis>Select the two</emphasis> answers that apply.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 5.14.1.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c560e6be-58d4-4a05-94bd-22d2063c7a09" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="Option 4: \(c(x)\), \(b(x)\), \(d(x)\), \(a(x)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;Option 1: \\(a(x)\\), \\(b(x)\\), \\(c(x)\\), \\(d(x)\\)&quot;,&quot;Option 2: \\(d(x)\\), \\(c(x)\\), \\(b(x)\\), \\(a(x)\\)&quot;,&quot;Option 3: \\(a(x)\\),\\(d(x)\\), \\(b(x)\\), \\(a(x)\\)&quot;,&quot;Option 4: \\(c(x)\\), \\(b(x)\\), \\(d(x)\\), \\(a(x)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Here are 4 equations defining 4 different functions, \(a, b, c\), and \(d\). List them in order of
          increasing rate of change. That is, start with the one that grows the slowest and end with the one that grows
          the quickest.
          <para>\(a(x)=5x+3\)</para>
            <para>\(b(x)=3x+5\)</para>
            <para>\(c(x)=x+4\)</para>
            <para>\(d(x)=1+4x\)</para>
          </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.14.3. 
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
